    "description": "Bring home a stunning collection of mid-century American art pottery with this 4-piece vintage Hull Art Pottery “Wildflower” lot, accompanied by two collector reference books by Sharon Loraine Felker. Known for its delicate matte pastel glazes and raised floral motifs, this collection showcases the iconic craftsmanship of Hull Pottery from Crooksville, Ohio.\nLot Details & Measurements:\n* Large Double-Handled Fan Vase: 11” tall. Marked on base: “Hull Art, USA, W-15-10.” Features a beautiful yellow-to-pink pastel ombr finish with molded floral details.\n* Ewer/Pitcher Vase: 6.5” tall. Marked on base: “Hull, W6-6, U.S.A.” Features a bulbous body, twisted vine-style handle, and pink-and-green floral design.\n* Double-Handled Urn Vase: 6.5” tall. Marked on base: “HULL, U.S.A., W-10-6” or similar Wildflower numbering. Features a soft pink upper section blending into a blue base with embossed floral accents. Similar in mold style to the Wildflower line.\n* Small Double-Handled Vase: 4.75” tall. Marked on base: “HULL, U.S.A., 405-4 3/4”. Features a fluted rim, yellow-to-blue gradient, and raised yellow floral accent.\nReference Books Included:\n* Lovely Hull Pottery by Sharon L. Felker spiral-bound.\n* Lovely Hull Pottery Book 2 by Sharon Loraine Felker.\nCondition: Pottery is in pre-owned vintage condition with vibrant colors and attractive display quality. Expect normal light wear consistent with age, along with minor manufacturing variations typical of vintage art pottery. Please review all photos for detailed views of each piece and its respective hallmarks. Books are in good collector condition with light shelf wear.\nA fantastic instant collection for both novice decorators and seasoned Hull pottery enthusiasts!",
